.DS_Store
*.sql
# ...but the theme seed is source, not a dump: it is generated from the old
# evaluateText() chain and the harness asserts against it. Blanket-ignored,
# it existed only on one laptop.
!dropship/dropship-themes-seed.sql
.claude/settings.local.json

# cardano.org submission assets (belong in the cardano-org fork, not here)
match3rpg.png
skulliance.webp

# Digital Hell Citizens 2: Fighters -- raw trait art from Maxingo, provided for
# the trait-assembly feature. Source art we were given, not something this repo
# should redistribute: it is large, it is another artist's unreleased work, and
# nothing here is deployment-ready yet. Keep it local until we know what shape
# the shipped assets take.
#
# TWO EXCEPTIONS, AND THE RULE BEHIND THEM: what is ignored here is the ARTIST'S
# work. Files WE author or generate are ours, and a file that only reaches the
# live site by somebody remembering to FTP it is a file that goes stale --
# trait-index.json sat 12 entries behind for exactly that reason, so ten new
# traits were live reading "Dh Samurai Helmet". Anything this repo maintains
# ships with this repo.
#
#   trait-index.json  -- display names, written by us, 28K
#
# THE NECK FILL IS NOT ON THAT LIST, AND IT WAS. Tracking it looked right by the
# same argument -- we generate it, so it is ours -- but it is ART IN PRACTICE:
# the 1000px block is drawn by hand in an image editor and re-drawn whenever the
# fit is off. Tracking a file that is edited outside the repo and uploaded by FTP
# means both channels write it, and git then reads the uploaded copy as a local
# modification and refuses to pull -- which is exactly what happened on the live
# server. One channel per file. This one is FTP, like the rest of the art.
#
# Git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, which is why
# this is a ladder of directory exclusions rather than one line.
dhc/*
!dhc/web/
dhc/web/*
!dhc/web/trait-index.json

# Generated Fighter composites -- rebuilt on demand, never source.
dhcrenders/
# Marquee-sized derivatives of those, for digihellcorps.php. Same rule.
images/dhc-fighters/

# Drop Ship art and audio live on the server, not in the repo -- see
# images-deployed-via-ftp. The harnesses plant probe files in these
# folders to drive the real code and remove them again; a fatal mid-run
# once left one behind and `git add -A` committed it, which then broke
# `git pull` on the live server because the real file was sitting there
# untracked.
dropship/sounds/
dropship/images/

# Secrets. Untracked was never the same as ignored: one `git add -A`
# from anybody who has these locally commits every credential on the
# platform, which is how a stray mp3 got in and broke git pull on the
# live server.
credentials/
